  "title": "utilpeek: stablecoin peg check (USDC, USDT, DAI, USDe, PYUSD) from on-chain Uniswap pools, in basis points"
 },
 "description": "utilpeek: Check stablecoin peg: is USDC, USDT, DAI, USDe or PYUSD holding its dollar peg. For supply by chain use get_stablecoin_supply. Returns whether USDC, USDT, DAI, USDe or PYUSD holds its dollar peg, from Ethereum Uniswap V3 pools: price_usd, deviation_bps, on_peg / watch / off_peg status (50 and 200 bps), the pools and their depth, and the read time. Indicative on-chain prices, not an oracle; non-USDC coins are priced in USDC and USDC by cross-check; pools read at most every 30 s; a failed coin is in `errors`; all coins failing is a 502 and an unknown coin a 422 (neither charged). Typically 1 to 4 s (one chain read), under 100 ms when cached. Price: USD 0.001. Free: 10 utilpeek calls per IP per UTC day. Docs: https://tanod.dev/learn/stablecoin-peg-check-api.html",
 "inputSchema": {
  "properties": {
   "coins": {
    "anyOf": [
